  "title": "Zheng-2024-theta-10.1038/s41562-024-01983-9",
  "description": "Microwire local field potentials (200 Hz) recorded from Behnke-Fried hybrid depth electrodes in 16 patients with drug-resistant epilepsy during a cognitive-boundary memory paradigm. Participants encoded 90 silent movie clips containing no, soft, or hard event boundaries, then completed scene-recognition and time-discrimination tests. Recording sites include the amygdala, hippocampus, and parahippocampal gyrus, with some participants also sampled in frontal regions. This iEEG-BIDS representation was converted from the authors' NWB release on DANDI (000940) without altering signal values.",
  "methods_description": "Broadband signals were recorded at 32 kHz (0.1-8000 Hz, Neuralynx ATLAS) from microwires of Behnke-Fried electrodes and downsampled by the authors to 200 Hz. LFPs were converted from NWB to BrainVision float32 microvolts with no filtering, resampling, re-referencing, cropping, or channel removal. Encoding, scene-recognition, and time-discrimination trials and TTL markers were mapped to BIDS events files.",
